In <1992Jul22.094859.12465@phillip.edu.au> t9114145@phillip.edu.au writes:

>In article <1992Jul21.172607.4988@tandem.com>, Brady_David@Tandem.Com (David Brady) writes:
>> 
>> I have a problem with my version of nethack (I believe it is J,  but I can't
>> look right now...)
>> 
>> Any sort of list on the screen is indented like 50 characters over (like
>> inventory) and when it says -More- and I press a key no more items are
>> displayed.  Every once in awhile the list will be displayed where it should be
>> (1st column) and works correctly.   Anyone else have a similiar problem?  And
>> how do you fix it?  This 'feature' almost makes the game unplayable on the Mac.
>>  Everything else seems to work fine.

>Someone correct me if I'm wrong, but I don't think your Nethack is broken -
>it's probably the fact that you're playing on a Mac. If the list of items
>is small enough then it will be displayed on the right hand side. Small enough
>means that it is less than one screen long and that you don't have entries like
>"a blessed +0 long sword named WHAT_A_LONG_NAME_IN_FACT_IT'S_HUGE_EVEN".
>If the list is more than a page long it gets displayed in column 1. Maybe
>you need a faster Mac, with more screen speed. I pity you if you're playing
>on a Plus - What's it like when you get a level with a Zoo?

Um, don't you think that the people who ported it to the Mac would have taken
into account the fact that it IS a Mac???  The screen size is not a problem,
since they use a font that fits 80x24 characters (exactly like UNIX, and
I've never seen this problem on UNIX).  I've never encountered this problem
on my Mac either, which leads me to believe that the copy of NetHack is 
corrupted somehow.  I could understand how this might be a problem on,
say, a Game Boy, but the Mac's screen isn't THAT small.

And yes, things do slow WAY down when you get a lot of monsters, but that's
the 68000 for you.

